      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "────────  COPY PROMPT BELOW  ────────"
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "Parity review after `bun run up --dry-run` (upstream upex-galaxy/agentic-qa-boilerplate@bf4c787, project lock fb5c9f2)."
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "Present the table below to the user, one row per finding, and WAIT for a decision per row"
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "(keep project | take upstream | merge) BEFORE editing anything. Then apply only the chosen rows,"
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "run tests -> types -> lint, and report."
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "Full diffs per row live in .agents/prompts/parity-plan.md; upstream copies: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/upex-galaxy/agentic-qa-boilerplate/main/<path>."
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "Rows marked BLOCKING failed a compatibility contract, or carry a hunk another file of this release depends on (the row says which gate proves it); both must be resolved before `bun run agents:compat:check` and the project gates pass."
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "`Now` is the copy on disk today: `kept` = the project's (a protected or project-declared path, never overwritten), `overwritten` = upstream's (the project's version is in the backup the row names), `-` = the row is not a contest between two copies."
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "`take upstream` is suggested only where the project lacks the content entirely; a row naming project-only servers, keys, headings or edits suggests `merge` (its backup or values are in the saved file)."
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "A `merge` row says what to port (upstream additions) and what to keep (project-only). A row labelled `informational` is a project identity file compared by keys only: merge = add the listed keys, never the values."
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "Nothing was applied: rows marked (resolved by apply) are the ones the real run fixes by itself (it rebuilds the generated surfaces), so this table lists MORE work than the run that applies. Do not plan manual edits from them."
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": ""
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "| # | Surface | File | Now | What differs (evidence) | Suggested |"
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "|---|---|---|---|---|---|"
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "| 1 | MCP | .codex/config.toml | kept | upstream added 1 key: \"mcp_servers.slack-aurora\"; nothing project-only; 1 hunk (+29/-0); Codex MCP registry (paired with .mcp.json / opencode.jsonc; `agents:compat:check` enforces parity across the three) | take upstream |"
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "| 2 | Hooks | .claude/settings.json | kept | same keys, \"permissions.allow\": same 71 item(s), order differs (port what you want, keep the rest); 5 hunks (+13/-13); project permissions and hook wiring; never overwritten | merge |"
    },
    {
      "ms": 17662,
      "text": "| 3 | Skills | .claude/skills | - | Claude skills alias missing: .claude/skills (resolved by apply) | run agents:compat (BLOCKING) |"
